  "limitations": [
    "All eight installations are qualification fixtures on the same previously used two-vCPU Linux arm64 Docker engine and physical Mac, alongside 21 unrelated QA containers. There are no existing user installations.",
    "Retirement is a stopped snapshot operation with explicit stop-work consent. Parked data and old credentials remain private recovery material. Retired names cannot be reused; capacity reuse assigns fresh node IDs and a disjoint namespace.",
    "The native startup sequence deliberately restarts the cold-test processes before normal ingress. Ephemeral process keys rotate across that restart; signed node, binary and storage claims remain bound to the independently selected policy. Key equality remains required while a process is unchanged.",
    "Recorded signature occurrences are verified with an independent Ed25519 implementation and policy hash checks, including lease/public-key agreement for active fleets. Unassigned bootstrap fleets instead require empty lease and deployment inventories. This is not hardware attestation.",
    "The earlier key-comparison failure and address-pool setup refusal remain unaccepted. Their existing resources were retained; no network or volume was pruned.",
    "This scenario does not qualify retirement beside another live cron, native process interruption during retirement, an I/O fault matrix, power loss, capacity limits or exactly-once external effects. The immutable runtime image and programs are unchanged. Raw credentials, logs, archives and application artifacts stay private."
  ],
